README file for xpilot5/inst/unix .

This directory contains the script fetchBuildXPilot5
who's cryptic name translates to "Fetch and Build XPilot5"
This script is designed to be run from outside the build tree
although it can be run from in the tree if you adjust either
the location of your source tree or edit the directory locations
inside of the file.

You should probably edit the directory locations anyway.

Caveat Emptor if the script updates itself during a `cvs update`.

This script has only been tested on Linux, but should port easily
to other *nix platforms.

ok:
Slackware 8.0.0
SuSe 8.2
SuSe 9.0
